+# Verification checklist: create-and-scene
+
+This is a merged verification plan, not executed verification. IDs retain both checklists' provenance; an original row covering several behaviors is cited on each applicable merged row. Source is `lead`, `implementor`, `both`, or `crosscheck` for coverage added from the approved definition. No implementation or verification result is claimed here.
+
+References are relative to `openspec/changes/create-and-scene/`: ESP = `specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md`, PS = `specs/presentation-skill/spec.md`, PV = `specs/presentation-verification/spec.md`. Project instructions refer to `AGENTS.md`. Rules refers to the lead's existing `acceptance-assumptions.md` rulings in the run output directory; canonical requirements remain authoritative. Checks include those rulings' concrete thresholds and hooks where applicable. Only INT-001, INT-002, E2E-001, and E2E-002 from `test-plan.md` are planned as integration or end-to-end tests. Skill procedure checks inspect instructions/templates rather than executing an agent journey. Screenshot diagnostics are advisory and do not establish visual quality by themselves.
